# The media player demo's third screen (docs/media-player-plan.md §6 step 5,
# M9, M13; docs/styling-pass-plan.md Y2): an album's header is its rounded
# cover, the title as a heading, the artist's link, then the year, track count
# and total time in words (the artist not repeated, M15; M16 (23)),
# a Play button and the favourite heart, over a gradient from the cover's
# most vivid colour (kaya.image_palette over the fetched bytes, the dominant
# when none is vivid) clamped by the core and fading into the window's
# ground, full bleed: the window gives no
# margin and the page gives its own back to the track table (M15). The dark
# leg runs this script under KAYA_APPEARANCE=dark. Play starts the album's first track; the heart
# is the app's, so it is still on when the album is opened again.
expect_image_phase image@art_201715 shown
click column@card_201715
expect_image_phase image@album_art shown
expect_shape image@album_art rounded
expect_ground column@album_header gradient
# M16 (35): the gradient's drawn top is the cover's vivid colour clamped by the core.
expect_ground_color column@album_header "light E3ABB9 dark 673946"
expect_inset 0
expect_inset column@album_tracks 16
expect_ax label@album_title "heading/Through The Olive Branches"
expect label@album_about "2021 · 2 songs, 40 sec"
expect_ax button@play_album "button/Play"
expect_ax checkbox@favorite "toggle/Favorite"
expect_checked checkbox@favorite off
toggle checkbox@favorite on
expect_checked checkbox@favorite on
# The favourites are kept in the app's preferences (M16 (24)).
expect_pref music.favorites "201715"
click button@play_album
expect_selected row@track[1860160] on
# The selected row's fill clears its cells by the platform's own cell padding
# and every cell sits on the row's centre (M19).
expect_row_inset row@track[1860160]
expect_row_centered row@track[1860160]
expect label@dock_title "Seven Chimes"
expect_ax button@play_pause "button/Pause"
expect_tint label@track_name[1860160] accent
expect_no_clipping
# The desktops go Home through the sidebar (docs/media-player-plan.md §1); a
# phone goes back (tools/lib/lanes/ios.py, android.py).
click row@go_home
expect_title "Home"
click column@card_581719
expect_title "Fellow Traveler"
expect_checked checkbox@favorite off
click row@saved[201715]
expect_checked checkbox@favorite on
toggle checkbox@favorite off
expect_checked checkbox@favorite off
expect_pref music.favorites ""
